  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67244,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours can occur on the visceral or parietal pleura {8827028; 19627540; 11015658; 2630775}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T12:23:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67245,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is usually found incidentally during surgery or at autopsy.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T12:23:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67246,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "<p>Adenomatoid tumour is extremely rare in the pleura, with &lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;cases described in the literature to date {19627540; 1676811; 8827028}. The age range is reported to be 40&ndash;70&nbsp;years. The role of asbestos exposure is unknown.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-05T15:39:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67247,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T12:23:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67248,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "<p>Adenomatoid tumours of the genital tract harbour somatic missense mutations in the <em>TRAF7</em> gene, a member of the family of TNF receptor&ndash;associated factors {29148537}, but this has not yet been identified in thoracic tumours. Adenomatoid tumours in the genital tract do not harbour alterations in <em>BAP1</em>, <em>NF2</em>, or <em>CDKN2A</em>&nbsp;{29148537; 20518890}. It is not known why adenomatoid tumours occur more frequently in the genital tract than in the serosal surfaces of the pleura {8827028}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-28T11:38:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67249,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>The tumour is an unencapsulated, relatively circumscribed, firm grey to yellow-tan nodule measuring 5&ndash;30 mm in greatest dimension {8827028; 11015658; 2630775}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-02T09:19:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67250,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours are circumscribed and nodular, arising on the pleural surfaces.&nbsp;Localized infiltration of surrounding soft tissues adjacent to the tumour may be seen. Combinations of interanastomosing pseudoglands, pseudovascular spaces, tubules, signet-ring&ndash;like spaces, and papillae lined by flat to cuboidal cells can be seen {8827028; 3517266}. The tumour cells have scant epithelioid or vacuolated cytoplasm and bland nuclei. Spaces may contain basophilic material. Vacuolated cells contain strands that bridge the lumina of the tubular and slit-like spaces and may form a fine network {14571427; 19543245}. Adenomatoid tumours often harbour lymphoid aggregates {14571427; 19543245}.</p>\r\n<p>Sampling the entire tumour is recommended to rule out epithelioid mesotheliomas with adenomatoid-appearing areas.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The tumour stains for cytokeratins and mesothelial cell markers, such as calretinin, D2-40, and WT1 {19543245; 17927601; 15891998; 14608532; 15084840}, with retained BAP1 expression {27813512; 30640754} (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/35/117\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em >Diffuse pleural mesothelioma</em>).</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The most important differential diagnosis is mesothelioma, which typically shows more diffuse pleural involvement and invasive growth as well as malignant histological characteristics such as cytological atypia, necrosis, or sarcomatoid patterns. Entities such as lymphangioma, epithelioid haemangioendothelioma, and metastatic signet-ring cell carcinoma should be excluded by immunohistochemistry.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-05T15:41:22"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
